"""ESP32-S3-MINI-1-N8 - ESP32-S3 Wi-Fi 802.11b/g/n and Bluetooth LE 5 module, 8 MB flash, PCB
antenna, 15.4 x 20.5 x 2.4 mm, 65 pads. Bare part.

Datasheet: Espressif ESP32-S3-MINI-1 & MINI-1U Datasheet v1.7 (the URL in pcb.toml), with the
ESP32-S3 Hardware Design Guidelines (schematic checklist, PCB layout design). Ordering code
ESP32-S3-MINI-1-N8: 8 MB quad flash, no PSRAM (Table 1-1); JLCPCB/LCSC C2913206. The -N4R2
variant ties IO26 to its PSRAM (Table 3-1 note b); on the -N8 IO26 is a free GPIO.

Pins (Table 3-1, Figure 3-1; the KiCad 10 RF_Module symbol uses the same numbers): 1, 2, 42, 43
and 46-65 GND (61 is the exposed pad, nine 1.2 mm squares in the footprint); 3 3V3; 4-25
IO0-IO21 (IO19 and IO20 are USB_D- and USB_D+, pads 23 and 24); 26 IO26; 27 IO47; 28 IO33;
29 IO34; 30 IO48; 31-37 IO35-IO41; 38 IO42; 39 TXD0 (GPIO43); 40 RXD0 (GPIO44); 41 IO45;
44 IO46; 45 EN. GPIO19/20 are exposed as the USB io: they are the only pins of the USB OTG and
USB-Serial/JTAG PHY (hardware design guidelines, USB). The default function of pads 28-29 and
31-33 is set by an eFuse (Table 3-1 note).

Supply (Tables 6-1, 6-2): VDD33 3.0-3.6 V (3.6 V absolute maximum), and the external supply
must deliver at least 0.5 A. Peak currents (Tables 6-4, 6-5): Wi-Fi TX 355 mA (802.11b at
20.5 dBm), 285-297 mA (g/n); RX 95-97 mA; Bluetooth LE TX 340 mA at 20 dBm, 204 mA at 9 dBm.
I/O (Table 6-3): VIH 0.75 x VDD, VIL 0.25 x VDD, VOH 0.8 x VDD, VOL 0.1 x VDD, 45 kOhm internal
pull-up/pull-down; EN resets the chip below 0.25 x VDD (VIL_nRST) and releases it above
0.75 x VDD (VIH_nRST).

Strapping pins (Table 4-1, section 4): GPIO0 (weak pull-up, boot mode with GPIO46: low at reset
enters the ROM download mode), GPIO3 (floating, JTAG source), GPIO45 (weak pull-down,
VDD_SPI voltage), GPIO46 (weak pull-down, boot mode and ROM message printing). They are sampled
when EN rises, with a 3 ms hold (Table 4-2). Keep host lines off them; the checklist recommends
a pull-up on GPIO0 and no large capacitor on it.

Integrator-owned circuitry (Figure 9-1, Peripheral Schematics; hardware design guidelines,
schematic checklist):
- 3V3: 22 uF and 0.1 uF in Figure 9-1; the board picks its bulk to suit its regulator.
- EN: never floating (Table 3-1); an RC delay, "usually R = 10 kOhm and C = 1 uF" (section 9),
  so EN rises after the 3.3 V rail; a reset button to GND.
- USB: GPIO19/20 to the connector; reserve 22-33 Ohm series resistors and unpopulated
  capacitors to GND close to the module (checklist, USB).
- UART: use a UART other than UART0 for application data, with a series resistor on the TX line
  to suppress harmonics (checklist, UART).
- Antenna (layout): the module edge with the antenna at the board edge, no copper, traces or
  parts under the antenna area on any layer (the footprint carries the keep-out), and clearance
  around it (PCB layout design guidelines).
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Usb2")

# Table 6-2: VDD33 3.0-3.6 V.
V3V3 = io(Power(voltage="3.0V to 3.6V"))
GND = io(Ground)
EN = io(Net)
USB = io(Usb2)
IO0 = io(Net)
IO1 = io(Net)
IO2 = io(Net)
IO3 = io(Net)
IO4 = io(Net)
IO5 = io(Net)
IO6 = io(Net)
IO7 = io(Net)
IO8 = io(Net)
IO9 = io(Net)
IO10 = io(Net)
IO11 = io(Net)
IO12 = io(Net)
IO13 = io(Net)
IO14 = io(Net)
IO15 = io(Net)
IO16 = io(Net)
IO17 = io(Net)
IO18 = io(Net)
IO21 = io(Net)
IO26 = io(Net)
IO33 = io(Net)
IO34 = io(Net)
IO35 = io(Net)
IO36 = io(Net)
IO37 = io(Net)
IO38 = io(Net)
IO39 = io(Net)
IO40 = io(Net)
IO41 = io(Net)
IO42 = io(Net)
IO43 = io(Net, help="TXD0, UART0 transmit (ROM boot messages)")
IO44 = io(Net, help="RXD0, UART0 receive")
IO45 = io(Net, help="strapping pin, VDD_SPI voltage (weak pull-down)")
IO46 = io(Net, help="strapping pin, boot mode and ROM printing (weak pull-down)")
IO47 = io(Net)
IO48 = io(Net)

Component(
    name="ESP32-S3-MINI-1",
    prefix="U",
    symbol=Symbol(library="ESP32-S3-MINI-1.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("ESP32-S3-MINI-1.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="ESP32-S3-MINI-1-N8", manufacturer="Espressif Systems"),
    pins={
        "GND": GND,
        "3V3": V3V3,
        "EN": EN,
        "USB_D-": USB.D.N,
        "USB_D+": USB.D.P,
        "IO0": IO0,
        "IO1": IO1,
        "IO2": IO2,
        "IO3": IO3,
        "IO4": IO4,
        "IO5": IO5,
        "IO6": IO6,
        "IO7": IO7,
        "IO8": IO8,
        "IO9": IO9,
        "IO10": IO10,
        "IO11": IO11,
        "IO12": IO12,
        "IO13": IO13,
        "IO14": IO14,
        "IO15": IO15,
        "IO16": IO16,
        "IO17": IO17,
        "IO18": IO18,
        "IO21": IO21,
        "IO26": IO26,
        "IO33": IO33,
        "IO34": IO34,
        "IO35": IO35,
        "IO36": IO36,
        "IO37": IO37,
        "IO38": IO38,
        "IO39": IO39,
        "IO40": IO40,
        "IO41": IO41,
        "IO42": IO42,
        "TXD0": IO43,
        "RXD0": IO44,
        "IO45": IO45,
        "IO46": IO46,
        "IO47": IO47,
        "IO48": IO48,
    },
)
